# text = Behold, I will speak unto you somewhat concerning Mosiah, who was made king over the land of Zarahemla; for behold, he being warned of the Lord that he should flee out of the land of Nephi, and as many as would hearken unto the voice of the Lord should also depart out of the land with him, into the wilderness--
# sent_id = 19
# llm_note = Complex sentence with an interrupted "for behold" subordinate clause. Root is "speak"(5). "Mosiah" is obl of "speak" (via "concerning"); "who was made king" acl:relcl on "Mosiah"; "for behold" introduces causal explanation: "he being warned..." is an absolute participial construction; "warned"(27) is the participial head, "he"(25) its nsubj; "that he should flee" (31-34) is a ccomp of "warned"; "and as many as would hearken...should also depart" is a conj clause sharing the broader "for behold" causal context; "as many as would hearken" — "many"(44) is head, "as...as" correlative relative; "should also depart" has "depart"(56) as head; "into the wilderness" obl of "depart"; "--" PUNCT trailing dash.
